  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive). Pattern: Xが{滅|ほろ}びる.\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR: {滅|ほろ}ぼす (to destroy, to annihilate).\n\nUSAGE:\n{滅|ほろ}びる describes large-scale destruction or extinction — civilizations falling, species dying out, kingdoms collapsing. It is not used for small everyday things breaking. The word carries a literary, dramatic tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {国|くに}が{滅|ほろ}びる: a country falls\n- {文明|ぶんめい}が{滅|ほろ}びる: a civilization perishes\n- {種|しゅ}が{滅|ほろ}びる: a species goes extinct\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n{滅亡|めつぼう}する is the する-verb equivalent meaning \"to perish/be annihilated,\" often used in news and historical writing.",
